    "final_answer": "Based on general maritime knowledge, fog horns typically operate at a frequency of approximately **180 Hz** (hertz). This low-frequency sound is ideal for fog horns because:\n\n- Low frequencies travel better through fog and over water\n- They can be heard from greater distances (often 5-10 miles or more)\n- The human ear is less affected by background noise at these frequencies\n\nThis ~180 Hz frequency is a standard for maritime fog signals, though some variations exist depending on the specific horn design and location."
